  "label": "The young man is mapped as the one who has lotion in the back",
  "description": "The bottom text 'i've got some lotion in the back.' creates an analogical mapping where the young man (visual entity) is implicitly identified as the person who possesses the lotion. The punchline relies on the visual of the young man (who appears to be offering nothing practical) being mapped onto the textual role of the lotion provider, creating a humorous contrast between his appearance and his 'offering'.",
